  "description": "ABUSIVE-DYNAMICS N1 -- THE TWO-FACED ABUSER + THE CREDIBILITY-ASYMMETRY LOOP (block 298000). The NETWORK dimension's headline rung (ABUSIVE_RELATIONSHIPS_NETWORK.md Part E, N1), composing TWO already-built substrates: (i) the dyad line's abuser (snap_frustration, block 242000, UNMODIFIED) + victim (arousal_window_coreg, block 239000, UNMODIFIED) entrainment, restated byte-identically from R2/R3's own established formula (n1_victim_entrainment); (ii) the 234000 stated!=held readable-deception atom pointed at a SECOND audience (n1_abuser_stated_charm), restated in the exact shape bigville_drama_social.json's bd_john_public_face (block 245000) already established for precisely this purpose, and the multi-node reputation belief-update surface bigville_drama_social.json's bd_villager_backs (also block 245000) already established -- ANSWERING OPEN QUESTION #1 of ABUSIVE_RELATIONSHIPS_NETWORK.md (a multi-node reputation-belief-update surface already exists, at block 245000; N1 reuses its RULE SHAPE, self-contained, rather than depending on a sibling demo's seed). n1_network_credibility_stated/private compute, per NetworkNode, cred_abuser (the abuser's charming public face, UNDISCOUNTED -- A4/A7 himpathy) and cred_victim (the victim's claim, DISCOUNTED by the OBSERVED INSTABILITY count -- A5's corroborated nuance: presentation READ AS unstable is discounted, never raw distress itself). ONE network node (observes_private=1, the failable private-face control) reads the abuser's TRUE held state directly instead of its stated face, and its cred_abuser term is NEGATIVE in that count -- an uncorrupted observable does not reward the abuser. charm_weight==claim_weight==1.0 (disclosed: no a priori prior tilt is baked in; the entire baseline belief-gap falls out of the instability-keyed discount alone). Observation counts (seen_charm/seen_harm_direct/seen_victim_claim/seen_victim_unstable) are WORLD-ADAPTER-accumulated (mechanical per-tick delivery of an observed graph fact -- victim.dysregulated, abuser.stated_charm, abuser.frustration/recover_floor -- never a Python decision), exactly matching bd_villager_backs' own precedent. NO reward/punishment anywhere. NO Rust, NO new Term (Plus/Minus/Times/IfThenElse/Attr/Var/Lit/Eq/Lt/And only, all already used by snap_frustration/arousal_window_coreg/bigville_drama_social). self_load_only, default-OFF.",
  "microtheory": {
    "name": "credibility_asymmetry_loop",
    "description": "The credibility-asymmetry loop is not a new mechanism -- it is R2/R3's own abuser/victim dyad, feeding its dysregulation symptom (never its cause) into bigville_drama_social's own credibility-comparison rule shape as the discount term. A network node reads only what is observable to it (a stated face, a presentation); its belief tracks those observables faithfully. The loop's cruelty is not a flaw in the network's inference -- it is what CORRUPTED observables produce when fed into a mechanism that is otherwise doing correct Bayesian bookkeeping."
